t use of oral contraceptive pills"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute Cholecystitis: Less likely due to absence of fever, leukocytosis, or gallstone risk factors", "Appendicitis: Atypical for right upper quadrant localization", "Gastrointestinal Bleed: No melena or hematemesis reported", "Alcoholic Hepatitis: Chronic alcohol use but acute presentation with hypotension is atypical"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension (80/40 mmHg)", "Tachycardia (110 bpm)", "Severe localized right upper quadrant tenderness"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecological Emergency with Hemodynamic Compromise", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.5388026523255409, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Lack of bleeding signs moderately reduces likelihood of conditions like Budd-Chiari syndrome."], "evidence_against": ["RUQ pain is atypical for ectopic pregnancy but not impossible in cases with atypical implantation or rupture."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Biliary Tract Obstruction", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.086, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of bleeding signs moderately reduces likelihood of conditions like Budd-Chiari syndrome."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Hepatic Venous Obstruction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.30196632163299547, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Lack of bleeding signs moderately reduces likelihood of conditions like Budd-Chiari syndrome."], "evidence_against": ["Absence of typical Bud